#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519644} :activity/id #uuid "c22e0dcd-15c2-55db-9d25-3bdc2b452a55" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050031 :topic/id #uuid "27615ef6-ec0e-5e91-b58b-24b70dc01a09" :topic/math-academy-id 3173} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519617 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aa7cb58-130b-52e2-9ffc-cc9e52330663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358818} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a9cb0c-c43b-5a83-8c67-e7c35f7eae70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359161} {:answer/id #uuid "ea13c98f-b638-5d97-8167-fa566662cb6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359835} {:answer/id #uuid "ec49dc46-0ba5-5fda-b9c2-6bec956ac528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359856} {:answer/id #uuid "f7162188-93f3-50e1-8684-87bec1a6cf00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359937}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359856} :answer-field/id #uuid "a955c8c5-959c-5957-86ce-5b5f4f04ba90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19a64e51-db17-58fb-852b-340494362842" :question/math-academy-id "q-95078" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x{y}^{2}),x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$ for $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x{y}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{2xy}{x{y}^{2}}=\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+2\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cot}⁡t-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1d1473e6-3651-50ed-9ec9-88f004e468cd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519623}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519619 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b80e388-89f0-55d3-9647-29eb1e7d21a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357986} {:answer/id #uuid "2931a144-34bf-5b91-9fd0-2c8561636d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s+{csc}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358129} {:answer/id #uuid "5f982da7-fadd-5a18-83b3-b5af485d42fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358586} {:answer/id #uuid "981660b8-6d8e-5d6b-a353-cc9e60ac0aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359084} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b01e60-3c8a-5b80-ab36-ad8a68a5308f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{sec}^{2}⁡2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359593}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357986} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce0a50c8-6fe1-52e2-992d-16da1ca6ce29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f22cdf5c-424c-5c09-91c4-a4b6bd7748c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95084" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y},x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s)+(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s})\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2-2\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2s}{{sin}^{2}⁡2s} \\\\  & =-2-2{cot}^{2}⁡2s \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1f2d63e2-db91-599f-ba79-b154350da4c1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519639}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519623 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "247ee7d0-904c-5d01-8297-06a98015037c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{s}}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385840} {:answer/id #uuid "7cec0dc1-33bb-5f04-a034-05527df9b19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+s){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385841} {:answer/id #uuid "323b91bd-668a-507d-8f83-8a04b4f2b115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2+\\sqrt{s}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385842} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd6bb8a-7411-5765-b787-90052e6b40f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385843} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbb05f2-b967-534b-9feb-494c22d63500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385844}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385844} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f70704d-2718-514e-b670-1b5ed75416ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c583feca-7024-59b3-b46e-988493997541" :question/math-academy-id "q-95083" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=y{e}^{x},$ $x=\\sqrt{s}$ and $y=s,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}$ for $s>0.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7e/7e5b5001794ecdf2c9b9e9102f334a63d2c59bc6f7511c2eb7fa358fc94cb0c5.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $s,$ where $x=x(s)$ and $y=y(s),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =s{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}s} \\\\  & =s{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{s}}+{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{s}}+{e}^{\\sqrt{s}} \\\\  & =(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{2}){e}^{\\sqrt{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2d471feb-727e-5216-935f-6bc8969b2a48" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519619}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519639 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e272a6d-78d3-5cb9-95c9-c87f0fea3da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357869} {:answer/id #uuid "34692782-e7a3-51e2-939e-c7595c3e9b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358219} {:answer/id #uuid "69e98fd7-fe36-540b-bd06-de9d5d7bdda7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})-\\frac{1+3{x}^{2}}{1+2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358677} {:answer/id #uuid "7b57f18a-b391-5d2a-a9af-d8d06a8a7f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)-\\frac{1+2{x}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358823} {:answer/id #uuid "9695921f-e190-55c7-a45b-cceb0f8f0066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359069}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357869} :answer-field/id #uuid "000855cc-b4eb-5315-a2d3-71276d48abd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "56630566-56de-5b10-a1f2-1989c1203d78" :question/math-academy-id "q-95121" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)$ and $y={x}^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ in the case where $y=y(x)$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+\\frac{x}{x+y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{x+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivative $y$ with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{x}{x+{x}^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x+2{x}^{2}}{x+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{x(1+2x)}{x(1+x)} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{x}^{2})+\\frac{1+2x}{1+x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6bc8b7a0-5c37-5a1c-8102-88692aa5f318"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519644 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1830bf59-5084-598f-b1f6-81191dfbfbcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2+t}{\\sqrt{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357965} {:answer/id #uuid "26a1cc25-ba10-5462-a7f5-4b6c422818d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358100} {:answer/id #uuid "72ac5140-e75a-5b93-834e-7afad4225743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358751} {:answer/id #uuid "8cdd033a-0457-5b60-bc47-43fcb08320c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358978} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddb28d7-a49c-5dad-b528-bbf182a53bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358988}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358988} :answer-field/id #uuid "146b2117-94cd-5963-92fa-afe7f73a78f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e0f22ddd-635a-5638-92e4-fbad8751067f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95077" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2xy},x=t$ and $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{2xy}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2xy}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}\\cdot 1+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{\\sqrt{2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "773b2d36-2f0a-57e0-8be2-e48bb09a4815" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519617}}] :activity/title "The Multivariable Chain Rule" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518986}]}
